atelier atelier/t270 "Put Cloudflare Access in front of the owner's pages (PAVI, 2026-10-07, after studying cloudflare/cloudflare-os): the Worker checks the cf-access-jwt-assertion header on every owner (non-/api) route with jose against https://TEAM.cloudflareaccess.com/cdn-cgi/access/certs, matching issuer (CF_ACCESS_ISS) and audience (CF_ACCESS_AUD), and keys the owner by the email claim matched to a configured owner email (as cloudflare-os wb/access.ts and wb/server.ts do); /login and its token form are refused when Access is configured (closing the unthrottled /login the 2026-10-06 audit found); /api/*, /showcase and /live.js stay outside Access (a Bypass policy), where agent and runner tokens are already enforced (src/index.ts); without CF_ACCESS_* set, today's token sign-in is unchanged so tests and other deployments keep working. Document the dashboard steps (create the Access application and its Bypass policy, set the two vars) in README for the owner; the session does not change account settings"
